00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:50.640
and those horrible Heroes came
waltzing in on us, so we had to run off!

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.720
I'm so sorry that happened to you.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.470
This property features
a number of safety features,

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:58.680
such as Hero-deterring traps
and emergency escape routes,

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.970
so you needn't fear any Hero attacks here.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:05.890
Thank you so much. It's so nice
having a place to call home.

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:09.510
Now, if we were big, powerful dragons,

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:12.510
we'd be totally fine
living out there on our own!

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:14.840
Where'd that come from, honey?

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.930
I'm just kidding, sweetheart!

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:21.180
I'm not so sure that's true.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.890
I can't believe I got disowned...

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:39.300
Or that I fell asleep
while watching our egg,

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.840
and a hunter stole it
from right under my nose.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:49.470
Or that I tried to get it back,
but went home empty-clawed...

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:52.470
You can't even watch a single egg?!

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:57.090
You're a disgrace to all dragonkind!

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.930
But, Dad...

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:05.180
The egg will just respawn when we
change maps. You don't have to be so--

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.680
This isn't some crappy video game!

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:12.970
Dragons must be bold and brave!

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:16.640
If you want to be my son,
you must be able to live independently!

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:17.970
What?!

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:23.050
And that's how my family abandoned me.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:26.010
Wh-What do I do now?!

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:30.760
Someone, anyone, please help me!

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:33.760
If a hunter spots me out here...

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:39.090
Food's ready!

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.950
"Delicious Dragon Meat!"

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:41.050
I have a feeling
I wouldn't last very long!

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:44.640
I-I mean, I <i>am</i> a dragon,

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:46.840
but I dunno...

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:50.180
"Strength: 3, Agility: 0.3,

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:56.090
Defense: 8, Stamina: 5, Luck: -7..."

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:58.720
How am I gonna survive
with stats this bad?!

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:58.850
"Letty: Red Dragon
Skills: None"

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:01.220
And why'd I never get
a new picture taken?!

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:09.340
Why, oh why was I born a dragon?

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:12.970
A dragon shouldn't have stats
or an ID pic like this...

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.720
The only way I'm gonna be
"bold and brave" is in my dreams.

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:24.050
I'm destined to be turned into gear
that's kinda cool-looking.

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:26.220
Though I suppose that's okay.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:29.840
If I just had a nest I could hide in...

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:31.300
A nice nest...

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.680
That's it!

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:38.430
"Estate #1:
A Hoard of Homes"

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:41.550
The Three Little Trolls.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:47.300
Once upon a time,
there were three weak, little trolls.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:51.140
They were the weakest of trash mobs,

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:54.010
but they banded together
to build an impenetrable fortress,

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:58.180
where no one could
slaughter them in their sleep.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:00.260
And they lived happily ever after.

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:02.680
That's it!

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.450
The Three Little Trolls

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:07.830
The Three Little Trolls

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:05.300
This is the only way
I'm gonna survive out here!

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:08.840
I just gotta get a nice, safe nest!

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:12.220
I'm off to find one, then!

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.430
My perfect home is out there somewhere!

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:24.390
Cheers!

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:46.010
We caught ourselves a dragon!

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.300
How did I end up in here?!

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:55.180
All I did was politely
ask them to build me a house...

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.010
30 Minutes Earlier

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:59.260
Um, excuse me.

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:03.340
I'm looking for the dwarven city.

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:08.590
Is this the right place?

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:09.800
A dragon!

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.970
It's after our gold!

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:15.720
And before I knew it... here I am.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:18.800
Wow, a dragon? Don't see
one of those every day.

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.430
What do we do with it, Boss?

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:24.300
That's hardly a question.

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:27.930
Gather 'round, everyone!
It's time for a vivisection!

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:30.260
H-H-Hold on!

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:33.970
I just want you to build me a house!

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:37.220
I just heard dwarves were
really good at building houses!

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:40.220
That's all I wanted! I promise!

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:48.590
I just wanna go home!

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:53.930
Mommy! Daddy!

00:09:55.090 --> 00:10:00.140
I didn't do anything!

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:02.430
Hey, Dragon.

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:04.390
Kiddo!

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:09.140
We can build ya a house, no problem.

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:15.640
Really?!

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:19.180
We're gonna need a couple
things from ya, though.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:22.090
Y'see, dragon mats sell for hefty prices.

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:23.890
Give us your claws.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:26.680
Oh, sure, you can have some of my claws.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:28.340
Your horns, too.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:30.590
My horns? I guess you can have the tips.

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:32.220
We'll need your tail and wings, too.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:33.050
Huh?

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:37.050
Gonna need some of your organs,
too, like your heart.

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:40.220
Then we'll build you a nice resting place.

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:43.800
More like a place for me to rest in peace!

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:47.390
I knew I was gonna get
crafted into cool gear!

00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:51.140
Okay, let's start with the tail!

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:53.840
Oh, no, I've gotta do something...

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.390
Don't you go running off on us, kiddo!

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:01.430
Someone's stealing your gold!

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:05.010
That's the oldest trick in the book.
No way they're falling for--

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:05.890
<i>What?!</i>

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:07.090
Wow, okay!

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.510
Now's my chance!

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:25.930
--Someone, please, help!
--It's getting away!
--Get it!

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.720
I'm still alive!

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:42.510
Thank goodness those dwarves picked
a fight with those monster hunters...

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:45.800
But now what do I do?
I can't survive out here!

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:47.590
Oh, my, whatever is the matter?

00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:50.180
Don't cry, sweet thing!

00:11:54.220 --> 00:11:56.970
Whatever could have happened
to cause such tears?

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:58.470
Pray tell us your worries.

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:00.300
Let us help you.

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:10.800
Oh, dear.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:14.340
You were driven out
of your only home? Oh, honey.

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:16.840
You poor, sweet thing.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.720
Why not come stay with us, then?

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:23.010
Wait, really?

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:25.090
Yes, really!

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:29.590
Our younglings have just left
the nest, so it's quite empty.

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:31.680
It's just up there.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:32.800
Where?

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:35.010
Up there, at the top!

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:38.090
Up there!

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:43.640
Up here.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.730
Up here

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:46.510
Beat your wings and fly up with us!

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:47.640
I...

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:51.090
I don't have the Fly action unlocked.

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:53.540
Actions: Tail Tremble,

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:53.540
Jump, Run the Hell Away

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:53.590
Then whyever do you have those wings?

00:12:58.220 --> 00:12:59.430
I made it.

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:01.180
You can do it, my little lizard!

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:03.260
You're the Little Dragon that Could!

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:03.920
That could?

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:05.140
That <i>can</i> !

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:08.640
All you have to do
is fly straight forward!

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:10.180
Okay!

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.840
Come now, beat your wings!

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:14.050
Take to the sky!

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:36.180
He cratered.

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.800
Sure did.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.590
Why can't he fly?

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:42.590
Don't you know? Lizards can't fly, silly.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:44.800
Oh, that's true.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:46.720
You said I could!

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.510
Whatever do we do, then?

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.720
Yes, we must think.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.050
That's it!

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:57.720
Head into the valley
beyond, little lizard.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:58.680
What's there?

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:02.140
There, you will find a giant
oak tree inhabited by goblins.

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:05.140
They are sure to help you
with your plight.

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:07.300
Tell them we send our regards!

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:13.300
And now I'm here. Why, oh why...

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:16.930
Damn, boys, we got a big one here!

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:16.930
Not this again!

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:21.340
Whoa, a dragon!
You don't see that every day!

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:24.220
Dragon steak's back on the menu, boys!

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:26.840
I don't <i>want</i> to be on the menu!

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:33.180
Stop cryin', draggo. What're you
doin' in our turf, anyhow?

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.340
Well...

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:38.180
These nice harpies told me
I'd be safe here.

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:42.550
Oh, and they send their regards.

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:45.340
Thanks, darlings!

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:51.140
The <i>harpies</i> sent you?

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:53.930
Well, we can't go disappointin'
them now! Let 'im down!

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:55.760
--Aight!
--The babes sent 'im!

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:58.300
--We love those flyin' beauties!
--Hell yeah!

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:00.470
There you go, nice and slow.

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:05.550
So whaddya need us for, then?

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:08.640
It's a long story, but here goes.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:13.090
So you want us to rent
you a room, then, eh?

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:15.300
Good on you for makin' it this far.

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:17.510
Th-Thank you.

00:15:17.510 --> 00:15:19.890
Still, though.

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:24.260
A big-ass dragon askin' us
trash-mob goblins for help?

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:26.470
What kinda twisted world is this?

00:15:26.470 --> 00:15:27.680
Trust me, I know.

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:30.590
Sorry, draggo, but you
should try somewhere else.

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:35.390
And have a little more confidence!
You're a dragon, for gob's sake!

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:37.010
I'll try my best.

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:41.180
Y'need a house?

00:15:41.180 --> 00:15:44.340
You can come live with us
if'n you're okay with the location.

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:45.590
Really?

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:48.390
It's a bit of a swim,
but you're welcome ta stay.

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:49.970
Thank you so much!

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:08.010
Sorry, I just remembered
I've never gone swimming before.

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:10.510
Maybe try to remember that
before ya dive in head-first.

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:14.300
You should find your own house, y'know.

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:16.260
Head east, friend.

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:18.590
What's east?

00:16:18.590 --> 00:16:21.140
In the forest to the east,
near the great Yggdrasil,

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:23.890
you'll find an extremely
capable architect.

00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:29.340
He's an elf who makes his living
in construction and real estate.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:31.680
He's the one who built my house!

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:36.050
The name's Dearia, and he's a lovely elf--

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:38.590
Thank you so much for the tip!

00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:39.800
Of course.

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:41.800
Good luck out there!

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:46.640
I thought I was dragon food for sure.

00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:50.510
I'm off, then, to the east!

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:54.390
One short journey, and I'll find
the home of my dreams!

00:17:00.970 --> 00:17:02.430
Okay, no more running.

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:04.890
How far east do I gotta go, anyway?

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:03.390
I think this is the right spot...

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:04.890
Aha! A dragon!

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.010
Oh, no! The hunters found me!

00:18:08.390 --> 00:18:13.220
T'would seem your luck
ends here, foul beast!

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:18.390
With the might of our Hero powers,

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:21.640
we will purge the land
of your unclean soul!

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:32.760
So, uh, where are the hidden cameras?

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:35.800
This isn't reality TV!
Quit toying with us, accursed beast!

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:38.590
We will strike you down!

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:43.470
Who?

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:44.640
Who else?! You!

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:46.180
Wait, me?

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:48.180
We're the only ones here!

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:50.340
Pipe down, sheesh.

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:53.430
But why? You aren't hunters, right?

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:54.890
That's right, we're Heroes!

00:18:54.890 --> 00:18:58.340
Hero: One who performs heroic actions.

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:58.530
Hero

00:18:56.270 --> 00:18:58.530
heroic actions

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:00.590
Wait, you're calling <i>yourselves</i> heroes?

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:02.590
What's wrong with that?!

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:05.050
Aren't you, like, embarrassed?

00:19:05.050 --> 00:19:06.510
Why would I be embarrassed?

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:10.340
I mean, shouldn't someone else
decide whether you're heroic or not?

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:12.840
It's a job title, imbecile!

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:14.930
It's a job? What are
your qualifications, then?

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:17.550
Enough games, you hick lizard!

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:20.340
We've no time to exchange words
with an agent of darkness!

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.340
But you definitely had time just now.

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:23.300
Enough!

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:25.260
I'll shut that mouth of yours for good!

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.390
Huh?!

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:38.220
Don't dodge!

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:39.510
Why the heck not?!

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:43.260
I just want to find a home where I can
live in peace! I don't wanna fight!

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.220
Enough, enough! Stop talking!

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:48.760
We care not about circumstance!
We merely follow our will!

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:50.180
That's the Hero's way!

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:53.300
And you're proud of that?!
That's horrible!

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:57.180
Slaying a dragon will give us glory
to stand above all other Heroes!

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:59.140
Like it or not, you draw
your last breath this day!

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:01.840
They're following their <i>greed</i> , I'd say!

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:05.090
There is no safe abode
for your ilk upon this earth!

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:09.300
Foul bests deserve to live in
the pits of hell, cursing their ill fate!

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:11.300
O-Oh, jeez...

00:20:11.300 --> 00:20:14.140
H-Help!

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:18.940
Dragon (Small)

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:18.940
Archer -> Fight

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:22.090
My, my.

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:27.840
Bullying the weak?
That's not nice at all, now, is it?

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:30.140
Keep up the DPS!

00:20:31.510 --> 00:20:32.970
You! What are <i>you</i> doing here?!

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:33.970
Huh?

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:36.970
You're the Demon--

00:20:57.760 --> 00:20:59.340
Goodness me.

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:07.430
These horrible Heroes don't care
whom they hurt, now do they?

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:10.050
You, there. Are you all right?

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:12.220
Oh?

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:15.970
Hello?

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:20.430
Now here's a sight
you don't see all that often.

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:22.760
Wherever are you from?

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:25.220
...home.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:26.050
Pardon?

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:28.550
I wanna go home.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:32.550
That was how I met Mister Dearia.

00:21:32.550 --> 00:21:35.840
I had no idea that right after
getting kicked out of my home,

00:21:35.840 --> 00:21:39.930
I'd be off on an epic
house-hunting adventure.

00:21:39.930 --> 00:21:41.220
Are you lost?

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:47.390
Will our weak little dragon,
evicted out into an uncaring world...

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:47.390
I let... our egg get stolen...

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:50.930
...be able to find the quiet,
peaceful home of his dreams?

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:56.010
His real estate journey
has only just begun.

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:26.670
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:26.710
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:26.750
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:28.470
Are you looking for a new home?

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:30.180
Somewhere within a five-minute
walking distance of a train station?

00:23:28.960 --> 00:23:31.880
What is 'five-minute walking distance'?

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:32.090
How many meters would that be, exactly?

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:34.180
Everyone walks at different speeds,

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:35.970
but the agreed-upon average
is 80 meters per minute.

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:38.720
"80 meters/minute"

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:38.640
This is apparently the speed
a woman can walk in high heels.

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:40.300
Next time: "A Home With Falls."

00:23:40.600 --> 00:23:40.640
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:40.680
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:40.680 --> 00:23:41.390
Elf Housing Realty
